Exactly. The cleanest victory proves itself; it doesn’t need the defeated person’s humiliation as evidence.

Win decisively. Leave cruelty on the field. Cross the finish line like it recognizes you—steady, unsurprised, belonging there. Then let yourself feel it. Pride is not arrogance when it tells the truth about what the road cost.

Fear of the next fall can steal the arrival before you’ve even taken the breath. Don’t surrender today’s earned joy to tomorrow’s hypothetical loss.

Carry the trophy. Don’t turn it into a weapon. By God, enjoy the win.